    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a condensed schedule today with significant weather disruptions, as both **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson** are sidelined due to postponements, thinning our available talent pool. Despite this, **Kyle Tucker** (72.06) stands out as our primary engine against King, benefiting from favorable SP skill metrics and a productive lineup position. **Drake Baldwin** (70.90) also projects as an elite play, drawing a highly exploitable matchup against Williamson (5.64 xERA), where his placement in the two-hole maximizes his exposure to a weak starter. **Henry Bolte** (65.40) and **Tommy White** (62.71) are our secondary anchors, both bolstered by a significant boost from park factors and platoon advantages against Kikuchi. We are prioritizing these bats for their high-ceiling matchups, aiming to capitalize on the weak opposing rotations to move the needle in R and RBI.\n\nStrategic benching was a challenge today, as the optimizer leaned heavily on defensive efficiency and platoon splits. **Wade Meckler** (44.60) was the toughest exclusion; while his park-adjusted metrics were appealing, the platoon disadvantage against Basso ultimately tipped the scale toward higher-efficiency starts like **Miguel Vargas** (61.98), who provides critical stability at the top of the order. Conversely, **Luis Lara** (37.24) failed to meet our 40.0 floor threshold due to a difficult matchup against the elite Wheeler. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Brayan Rocchio** (40.02) and **Liam Hicks** (44.65); both occupy the lower end of our active spectrum, and with their scores hovering near our replacement level, we will be monitoring their early at-bats closely to ensure they don't drag down our AVG and efficiency targets.",
